{"labeler": "bde20ef8-f6b3-4e84-b018-dc6aba6c80ee", "timestamp": "2022-11-14T22:19:46.176700", "generation": 6, "is_quality_control_question": false, "is_initial_screening_question": false, "question": {"problem": "If\n\\[f(n + 1) = (-1)^{n + 1} n - 2f(n)\\]for $n \\ge 1,$ and $f(1) = f(1986),$ compute\n\\[f(1) + f(2) + f(3) + \\dots + f(1985).\\]", "ground_truth_solution": "We can list the equations\n\\begin{align*}\nf(2) &= 1 - 2f(1), \\\\\nf(3) &= -2 - 2f(2), \\\\\nf(4) &= 3 - 2f(3), \\\\\nf(5) &= -4 - 2f(4), \\\\\n&\\dots, \\\\\nf(1985) &= -1984 - 2f(1984), \\\\\nf(1986) &= 1985 - 2f(1985).\n\\end{align*}Adding these equations, we get\n\\[f(2) + f(3) + \\dots + f(1986) = (1 - 2 + 3 - 4 + \\dots + 1983 - 1984 + 1985) - 2f(1) - 2f(2) - \\dots - 2f(1985).\\]To find $1 - 2 + 3 - 4 + \\dots + 1983 - 1984 + 1985,$ we can pair the terms\n\\begin{align*}\n1 - 2 + 3 - 4 + \\dots + 1983 - 1984 + 1985 &= (1 - 2) + (3 - 4) + \\dots + (1983 - 1984) + 1985 \\\\\n&= (-1) + (-1) + \\dots + (-1) + 1985 \\\\\n&= -\\frac{1984}{2} + 1985 \\\\\n&= 993.\n\\end{align*}Hence,\n\\[f(2) + f(3) + \\dots + f(1986) = 993 - 2f(1) - 2f(2) - \\dots - 2f(1985).\\]Then\n\\[2f(1) + 3f(2) + 3f(3) + \\dots + 3f(1985) + f(1986) = 993.\\]Since $f(1986) = f(1),$\n\\[3f(1) + 3f(2) + 3f(3) + \\dots + 3f(1985) = 993.\\]Therefore, $f(1) + f(2) + f(3) + \\dots + f(1985) = \\boxed{331}.$", "ground_truth_answer": "331", "pre_generated_steps": ["This looks like a tricky recursive function.", "I wonder if I can find a pattern or a closed form for f(n).", "Let me start by plugging in some small values of n and see what happens.", "If n = 1, then f(2) = (-1)^2 * 1 - 2f(1) = 1 - 2f(1).", "If n = 2, then f(3) = (-1)^3 * 2 - 2f(2) = -2 - 2(1 - 2f(1)) = -4 + 4f(1).", "If n = 3, then f(4) = (-1)^4 * 3 - 2f(3) = 3 - 2(-4 + 4f(1)) = 11 - 8f(1).", "I see a pattern emerging.", "It looks like f(n) alternates between positive and negative terms, and the coefficient of f(1) is always 2^(n-1), while the constant term is a multiple of n.", "I can guess a general formula for f(n) based on this pattern:\n\n\\[f(n) = (-1)^n \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} - 2^{n-1} f(1)\\]", "To check if this formula is correct, I can plug it into the original recursion and see if it satisfies it.", "I get:\n\n\\[f(n+1) = (-1)^{n+1} \\frac{(n+1)(n+2)}{2} - 2^n f(1)\\]\n\n\\[= (-1)^{n+1} n - 2 \\left( (-1)^n \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} - 2^{n-1} f(1) \\right)\\]\n\n\\[= (-1)^{n+1} n - 2f(n)\\]", "So the formula works!", "Now I can use it to compute the sum of f(1) + f(2) + ... + f(1985).", "I notice that f(1) = f(1986), so the sum is actually the same as f(1) + f(2) + ... + f(1986).", "I can group the terms in pairs of odd and even indices, and use the fact that f(n) + f(n+1) = (-1)^n n, which follows from the recursion.", "So the sum becomes:\n\n\\[f(1) + f(2) + ... + f(1986) = (f(1) + f(2)) + (f(3) + f(4)) + ... + (f(1985) + f(1986))\\]\n\n\\[= 1 + 3 + 5 + ... + 1985\\]", "This is an arithmetic series with 993 terms, common difference 2, and first term 1.", "I can use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n\\[S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a_1 + a_n)\\]", "In this case, n = 993, a_1 = 1, and a_n = 1985.", "So the sum is:\n\n\\[S_{993} = \\frac{993}{2} (1 + 1985) = 986 \\times 993\\]\n\n# Answer\n\n986 \\times 993"], "pre_generated_answer": "986 \\times 993", "pre_generated_verifier_score": 7.638672301425164e-05}, "label": {"steps": [{"completions": [{"text": "This looks like a tricky recursive function.", "rating": 0, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "I wonder if I can find a pattern or a closed form for f(n).", "rating": 0, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "Let me start by plugging in some small values of n and see what happens.", "rating": 0, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "If n = 1, then f(2) = (-1)^2 * 1 - 2f(1) = 1 - 2f(1).", "rating"