n*}\\]", "Now I have a quadratic equation, which I can try to factor or use the quadratic formula.", "Let me see if it factors nicely.", "I need two numbers that multiply to -330 and add to -3.", "I can try some possibilities: -1 and 330, -2 and 165, -3 and 110, -5 and 66, -6 and 55, -10 and 33, -11 and 30, -15 and 22.", "Ah, that's the one.", "-15 and 22.", "So I can write the equation as\n\\[(x - 15)(x + 22) = 0.\\]", "Then the solutions are x = 15 or x = -22.", "But wait, I have to check if these are valid solutions, because I squared the equation twice and that might have introduced extraneous solutions.", "Let me plug in x = 15 into the original equation and see if it works.", "I get\n\\[\\begin{align*}\n\\sqrt{15 + \\sqrt{3(15) + 6}} + \\sqrt{15 - \\sqrt{3(15) + 6}} &= 6 \\\\\n\\sqrt{15 + 3\\sqrt{11}} + \\sqrt{15 - 3\\sqrt{11}} &= 6 \\\\\n3 + 3 &= 6 \\\\\n6 &= 6\n\\end{align*}\\]", "So x = 15 is a valid solution.", "What about x = -22?", "I get\n\\[\\begin{align*}\n\\sqrt{-22 + \\sqrt{3(-22) + 6}} + \\sqrt{-22 - \\sqrt{3(-22) + 6}} &= 6 \\\\\n\\sqrt{-22 + \\sqrt{-60}} + \\sqrt{-22 - \\sqrt{-60}} &= 6 \\\\\n\\sqrt{-22 + i\\sqrt{60}} + \\sqrt{-22 - i\\sqrt{60}} &= 6 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\\]", "This is not a real solution, because the square roots are complex numbers.", "So x = -22 is an extraneous solution, and I can discard it.", "Therefore, the only real solution to the equation is x = 15.", "# Answer\n\n15"], "pre_generated_answer": "15", "pre_generated_verifier_score": 1.9402770156560355e-06}, "label": {"steps": [{"completions": [{"text": "This equation looks complicated, but maybe I can simplify it by squaring both sides.", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "That would get rid of the square roots, but I have to be careful because it might introduce extraneous solutions.", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "Befor