{"labeler": "2b794369-78c8-4e28-b3ba-eb0dd4a9ab2c", "timestamp": "2022-11-13T05:12:15.166550", "generation": 6, "is_quality_control_question": false, "is_initial_screening_question": false, "question": {"problem": "Consider the function $z(x,y)$ describing the paraboloid\n\\[z = (2x - y)^2 - 2y^2 - 3y.\\]Archimedes and Brahmagupta are playing a game.  Archimedes first chooses $x.$  Afterwards, Brahmagupta chooses $y.$  Archimedes wishes to minimize $z$ while Brahmagupta wishes to maximize $z.$  Assuming that Brahmagupta will play optimally, what value of $x$ should Archimedes choose?", "ground_truth_solution": "Expanding $z,$ we get\n\\begin{align*}\nz &= 4x^2 - 4xy + y^2 - 2y^2 - 3y \\\\\n&= -y^2 - (4x + 3) y + 4x^2.\n\\end{align*}After Archimedes chooses $x,$ Brahmagupta will choose\n\\[y = -\\frac{4x + 3}{2}\\]in order to maximize $z.$  Then\n\\begin{align*}\nz &= -\\left( -\\frac{4x + 3}{2} \\right)^2 - (4x + 3) \\left( -\\frac{4x + 3}{2} \\right)^2 + 4x^2 \\\\\n&= 8x^2 + 6x + \\frac{9}{4}.\n\\end{align*}To minimize this expression, Archimedes should choose $x = -\\frac{6}{16} = \\boxed{-\\frac{3}{8}}.$", "ground_truth_answer": "-\\frac{3}{8}", "pre_generated_steps": ["I need to find a value of $x$ that minimizes the maximum possible value of $z.$", "To do that, I first need to find out how Brahmagupta will choose $y$ given any value of $x.$", "I notice that $z$ is a quadratic function of $y,$ and its coefficient of $y^2$ is always negative, regardless of $x.$", "This means that $z$ has a maximum value with respect to $y$ when $y$ is equal to the negative of the coefficient of $y$ divided by twice the coefficient of $y^2.$", "In other words, the optimal choice of $y$ for Brahmagupta is\n\\[y = -\\frac{2(2x - 1)}{2(-2)} = x - \\frac{1}{2}.\\]", "If I plug this value of $y$ into $z,$ I get the maximum value of $z$ that Brahmagupta can achieve given $x,$ which I will call $w(x).$", "\\[w(x) = z(x, x - \\frac{1}{2}) = (2x - (x - \\frac{1}{2}))^2 - 2(x - \\frac{1}{2})^2 - 3(x - \\frac{1}{2})\\]", "I simplify this expression by expanding and combining like terms.", "\\[w(x) = (\\frac{3}{2}x + \\frac{1}{4})^2 - 2(\\frac{x^2}{4} - \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{1}{16}) - 3x + \\frac{3}{2}\\]\n\\[w(x) = \\frac{9}{4}x^2 + \\frac{3}{2}x + \\frac{1}{16} - \\frac{x^2}{2} + x - \\frac{1}{8} - 3x + \\frac{3}{2}\\]\n\\[w(x) = \\frac{5}{4}x^2 - \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{9}{16}\\]", "Now I have a quadratic function of $x$ that represents the maximum value of $z$ that Brahmagupta can achieve given any value of $x.$", "I want to find the value of $x$ that minimizes this function.", "I notice that the coefficient of $x^2$ is positive, which means that the function has a minimum value.", "I also know that the minimum value of a quadratic function occurs when $x$ is equal to the negative of the coefficient of $x$ divided by twice the coefficient of $x^2.$", "In other words, the optimal choice of $x$ for Archimedes is\n\\[x = -\\frac{-\\frac{1}{2}}{2(\\frac{5}{4})} = \\frac{1}{5}.\\]", "# Answer\n\n1/5"], "pre_generated_answer": "1/5", "pre_generated_verifier_score": 0.004172327498040665}, "label": {"steps": [{"completions": [{"text": "I need to find a value of $x$ that minimizes the maximum possible value of $z.$", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "To do that, I first need to find out how Brahmagupta will choose $y$ given any value of $x.$", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "I notice that $z$ is a quadratic function of $y,$ and its coefficient of $y^2$ is always negative, regardless of $x.$", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "This means that $z$ has a maximum value with respect to $y$ when $y$ is equal to the negative of the coefficient of $y$ divided by twice the coefficient of $y^2.$", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completi