 = (p-15)+15 = p$ and $f(15) = (p-15)+p = 2p-15.$", "In this case, $f(p)$ is smaller than $f(15),$ so the minimum value of $f(x)$ is $f(p) = p.$", "Therefore, the minimum value of $f(x)$ depends on the value of $p.$", "If $p \\leq 7.5,$ then the minimum is $15.$", "If $p > 7.5,$ then the minimum is $p.$", "# Answer\n\n15 or p"], "pre_generated_answer": "15 or p", "pre_generated_verifier_score": 8.393961395777703e-09}, "label": {"steps": [{"completions": [{"text": "I notice that $f(x)$ is a sum of three absolute value functions, which are piecewise linear.", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "This means that $f(x)$ is also piecewise linear, and its graph consists of line segments with different slopes.", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "To find the minimum value of $f(x),$ I need to identify the points where the slope of $f(x)$ changes, and compare the function values at those points.", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "The slope changes occur when $x$ equals the arguments of the absolute value functions, namely $p, 15,$ and $p+15.$", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "However, since the domain of $x$ is restricted to the interval $p \\leq x \\leq 15,$ I only need to consider the points $x=p$ and $x=15.$", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "These are the endpoints of the domain, and also the points where two of the absolute value functions change from positive to negative or vice versa.", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "To find the function values at these points, I plug them into $f(x).$", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}